The test method sets `to_numpy_dispatch` using `hash("absmax-profile") ^ hash("dispatch-probe")`, then passes that boolean as `to_numpy` into `quantizers.abs_max_quantize`. Because Python string hashes are randomized across interpreter runs, that boolean is not fixed across repeated executions. In `abs_max_quantize`, the `if to_numpy:` branch and the `else` path execute different source lines before returning, so the ordered `(call|line|return)` line-number sequence can change from run to run. Therefore no exact path-sequence invariant exists across all runs.

## Answer
{"invariant_exists":false}
